        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "54e05598-0dc8-50ae-b556-cb04f3d988d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Carpentaria acuminata, Carpentaria, Panax, ginseng\n- Plant families: Araliaceae\n- Places: Northern Territory, Australia, Gulf of Carpentaria, Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System\n\nFacts:\n- Carpentaria acuminata, also called the carpentaria palm, is the only species in the genus Carpentaria.\n- Carpentaria acuminata is native to tropical coastal regions in the north of the Northern Territory, Australia.\n- Panax, the ginseng genus, belongs to the Araliaceae family.\n- The Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System comprises a 994 km tract of tidal wetlands on the south-west coast of the Gulf of Carpentaria in the Northern Territory of Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
